# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion SHIP gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/fusion-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6nt-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the approved commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s6nt-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# G1 (STOP): the card re-test of the SHIP image, unaudited (an audited 8x262k profile costs about 8.4 minutes per request): the ship profile with W2, engine reuse and the
# op-fusion levers together for the first time on the traffic profile. Warmup, a coding answer, eight-seat steady and skew (the deadline rule: slowest first token under 238
# s), the cold 262k stall shape, the five Lever N hang shapes, the drain, an abort and reuse of a parked slot, then the 40 agent turns of parked_turns. RUN WITH THE CI
# PAUSED (the skew is timed). READ (c2_smoke_check, every rule clean, including the smoke's concurrent8_steady list rule and the fusion rules): '[QWEN-C2] profile
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt: OWNER TRAFFIC WAIVER', 'lever N governor: ttft=180 gap_floor=8', the tp4 sdpa multi engaged line and its
# UNQUALIFIED line (expected at 262,144), the conv-gates spread engaged line, EVERY op-fusion lever's engaged line and no fell-back line (QWEN_C2_TEXT_ONLY_BOOT,
# QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_DIAG_TRIM, QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEAN, QWEN_FAST_BATCHED_READS, QWEN_FAST_CCL_OPTIONS, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_GATEUP1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_HEAD64,
# QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_MM_GRID, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_PERMUTE, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_QKV1, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_REDUCE, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_TAIL, QWEN_FAST_GRID13, QWEN_FAST_KV_PAGE_WRITER,
# QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_ADAPTIVE, QWEN_FAST_MLP_CFG, QWEN_FAST_OCTO, QWEN_FAST_OCTO_ATTN_BUNDLE, QWEN_FAST_OCTO_DRAFT, QWEN_FAST_OCTO_GLUE8, QWEN_FAST_OCTO_MIN_LIVE,
# QWEN_FAST_OCTO_WAIVER, QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_HANDOFF, QWEN_FAST_PRESTAGE_DIFF, QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ, QWEN_FAST_SOLO_PACKED, QWEN_FAST_TAP_WINDOW_ALIGNED,
# QWEN_FAST_TP4_GDN_WC, QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX, QWEN_FAST_WRITE_PACKED_LEAN, QWEN_PREFIX_CKPT_PRECONVERTED, QWEN_PREFIX_CKPT_PRECONVERTED_AUDIT,
# QWEN_PREFIX_STICKY_UNDROP, QWEN_PREFIX_STORE_GIB, QWEN_PREFIX_WINDOW_CARRY), the round-host engaged line with select and read taken on at least 95 percent of the drafting
# steps, the parked build of 8 engines at 0.41-0.51 GB each (parked_judge's lever band; 0.418 measured) and every rebind clean, no stall, 0 crashes, skew under 238 s, the
# DRAM-after-attach lines (record the free DRAM per chip). TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a
# second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter holding it, power, current, temperature, kernel NOPs); read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result;
# the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs on the host and reads only. CHECKPOINT (C2_MODEL_REPO and C2_MODEL_REVISION, qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): the job
# serves ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b at b4c84d42903a, the checkpoint production serves beside this profile, from its own converted-weight directory and with its catalog
# entry's request numbers laid over the profile's (serving_c2_contract.checkpoint_limits: the default answer and the output ceiling), as a production boot runs; the keys
# are the same in G1, GX0, GX1 and G2, so GX0 and GX1 differ by the profile alone. READ: the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=..." once, a "weight cache ...: found" line and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..."
# line (the smoke step passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint; the prefix gate checks every arm's log). NO-TIER READ (tp4/s6-notier): no "host tier on" line and no
# "host tier restore slice on" line; the checkpoint store at 16 GiB; the "[PINDIAG] text-only boot: vision tower skipped" line once per engine process and no vision weight
# load in the boot log; the "[PINDIAG] host heap trimmed after warmup" line once (or its skipped line, never a traceback); every other ship-6 read unchanged (the governor's
# install line, WC's engaged line and its one octo decline). Duration (estimate): 60 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s6nt-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6-nt
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_skew,stall8_cold262k,levern_decoder_finishes,levern_all_decoders_finish,levern_cancel_mid_prefill,levern_arrival_during_prefill,levern_seed_stops,concurrent8_drain,parked_abort_reuse,parked_turns
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
C2_TELEMETRY=1
